%U A398211 2,2,7,1,2,4,6,4,9,7,0,3,1,9,0,3,8,6,5,4,3,6
%N A398211 Decimal expansion of the surface area of a canonical (dual-uniform) octagonal trapezohedron with unit short edge length.
%C A398211 The octagonal trapezohedron is the dual polyhedron of the octagonal antiprism.
%H A398211 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A398211/b398211.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 2..10000</a>
%H A398211 David I. McCooey, <a href="https://dmccooey.com/polyhedra/OctagonalTrapezohedron.html">Octagonal Trapezohedron</a>.
%H A398211 Polytope Wiki, <a href="https://polytope.miraheze.org/wiki/Octagonal_antitegum">Octagonal antitegum</a>.
%H A398211 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Trapezohedron.html">Trapezohedron</a>.
%H A398211 <a href="/index/Al#algebraic_08">Index entries for algebraic numbers, degree 8</a>.
%F A398211 Equals 2*sqrt(1 + 4*cos(Pi/8) - sqrt(2))*csc(Pi/16)^2 = 2*sqrt(1 + 4*A144981 - A002193)*csc(Pi/16)^2.
%F A398211 Equals the largest real root of x^8 - 9216*x^6 + 1404928*x^4 + 16777216*x^2 - 197132288.
%e A398211 95.187915423042003260593083703239926841483516710404...
%t A398211 First[RealDigits[2*Sqrt[1 + 4*Cos[Pi/8] - Sqrt[2]]*Csc[Pi/16]^2, 10, 100]]
%t A398211 (* Alternative: *)
%t A398211 First[RealDigits[PolyhedronData[{"Trapezohedron", 8}, "SurfaceArea"], 10, 100]]
%Y A398211 Cf. A398210 (volume), A398212 (inradius), A398213 (midradius), A398214 (height).
%Y A398211 Cf. A398215 (long edge).
%Y A398211 Cf. A398216 (small face angle), A398217 (large face angle), A398218 (dihedral angle).
%Y A398211 Cf. A394535 (surface area of the dual).
%Y A398211 Cf. A002193, A144981.
%K A398211 nonn,cons,easy
